      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are right to be skeptical; these \"friend-shoring\" strategies often blur the line between national security and disguised protectionism, frequently shielding inefficient domestic industries. While the intent is risk reduction, the practical result is often higher prices and reduced consumption for global consumers, effectively undermining the cost efficiencies that defined the golden age of globalization. Ultimately, the transition is a painful trade-off where the gains in security and stability may not outweigh the long-term costs of slower economic growth.",
      "source": "target",
